From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 07:24:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: preserve DFS state for unchanged regulatory rules

Creating a VIF rebuilds the regulatory rules for the shared wiphy. Even
when those rules are identical, applying them resets cfg80211 DFS state.
On a three-radio SBE1V1K, recreating the 6 GHz AP turns the active 5 GHz
160 MHz channel from DFS_AVAILABLE into DFS_USABLE. Subsequent beacon
updates fail with -EINVAL and can leave hostapd color changes stuck.

Compare the complete regulatory identity and rule array under RCU before
applying a steady-state update. Skip only an exact duplicate, preserving
country, power, bandwidth, DFS and WMM rule changes. Still apply updates
during initialization and firmware recovery.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/reg.c
@@ -264,6 +264,25 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < regd_orig->n_reg_rules; i++)
 		memcpy(&regd_copy->reg_rules[i], &regd_orig->reg_rules[i],
 		       sizeof(struct ieee80211_reg_rule));
+}
+
+static bool ath12k_regd_is_current(struct wiphy *wiphy,
+				   const struct ieee80211_regdomain *regd)
+{
+	const struct ieee80211_regdomain *wiphy_regd;
+	bool equal = false;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	wiphy_regd = rcu_dereference(wiphy->regd);
+	if (wiphy_regd && wiphy_regd->n_reg_rules == regd->n_reg_rules &&
+	    wiphy_regd->dfs_region == regd->dfs_region &&
+	    !memcmp(wiphy_regd->alpha2, regd->alpha2, sizeof(regd->alpha2)) &&
+	    !memcmp(wiphy_regd->reg_rules, regd->reg_rules,
+		    regd->n_reg_rules * sizeof(regd->reg_rules[0])))
+		equal = true;
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return equal;
 }
 
 int ath12k_regd_update(struct ath12k *ar, bool init)
@@ -391,7 +410,14 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	ret = regulatory_set_wiphy_regd(hw->wiphy, regd_copy);
+	/* Adding a VIF can regenerate unchanged rules for a shared wiphy.
+	 * Reapplying them discards DFS availability established by another
+	 * radio. Keep startup/recovery and every actual rule change intact.
+	 */
+	ret = 0;
+	if (init || ah->state != ATH12K_HW_STATE_ON ||
+	    !ath12k_regd_is_current(hw->wiphy, regd_copy))
+		ret = regulatory_set_wiphy_regd(hw->wiphy, regd_copy);
 
 	kfree(regd_copy);
 
